        "procedure": "Shared procedure for 1–3: HL (0.04 mmol) in methanol (20 mL) was treated with Ln(acac)3·2H2O (0.04 mmol; Ln = Eu for 1) dissolved in dichloromethane (5 mL). The mixture was stirred at room temperature for 30 min, then heated under reflux for 3 h to give a light-yellow solution, cooled to room temperature, filtered, and left unperturbed to evaporate slowly. After about one week, yellow block-shaped crystals suitable for X-ray diffraction were obtained.",
